**Also unverified — no frontend test infrastructure exists in this repo.** `frontend/package.json` has no `test` script and no test runner (`vitest`, `@testing-library/react`, etc.) is installed; `git log` shows no frontend test file has ever been added across the prior 8 feature cycles (search, priority, due-date, clear-completed, etc.), despite `CLAUDE.md` mentioning `npm test`. I followed that established precedent rather than introducing new test infra as a side effect of this ticket — flagging for the reviewer/product-manager rather than silently deciding it, since it's a repo-wide gap, not specific to this feature.

**How to verify manually:** `cd frontend && npm run dev`, then in the browser: delete a task → row disappears immediately, toast appears bottom-center with title + Undo (AC1); click Undo within 5s → row reappears with priority/due-date/done-state intact (AC2, AC4); let it expire → toast auto-dismisses and a page refresh shows the task gone (AC3); delete two tasks and undo only one (AC5); delete a task, then trigger "Clear completed" on a different done task before the first expires, and confirm no error banner appears once the first's window lapses (AC6).